@bank all
// Writer 5, for social B2: missing a friend who moved on (bond:missed; {missed} is their closest friend who left the
// Wren; a line with no such bond is skipped). Warm, a little wistful, light. {missed} has no known pronouns: name only.

== smalltalk
? bond:missed
- {missed} would've laughed at that.   #funny
- Still save a seat for {missed}. Habit.
- Letter from {missed} today. Two pages.   #warm
- {missed} always had the last biscuit. Now I do.   #funny
- Wonder what {missed} is having for dinner.
? bond:missed act:meal
- This was {missed}'s favourite. Still is, probably.
? bond:missed trad:quiz
- {missed} knew every answer in this round.   #funny
? bond:missed time:evening
- {missed} would be telling a story about now.

== feel
? bond:missed
- I'm all right. Bit quiet without {missed}. You get used to it. Slowly.
- Wrote to {missed} last night. Three pages. Mostly about the food.   #funny
- {missed} says the new ship's fine. Bigger. Colder. Nobody makes tea like Brennan.   #funny
? bond:missed tier>=acquaintance
- Funny. I still turn round to tell {missed} things. Then I tell you instead.   #warm
? bond:missed mood:low tier>=friend
- Missing {missed} today. That's all. Sit a minute? That helps.   #warm
? bond:missed mood:high
- Good day! {missed} wrote back. Settling in fine, apparently.   #warm
? bond:missed tier>=colleague
- {missed} left me a mug. I use it every morning. Don't tell anyone.   #warm
